.TH DQL 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql \- DelightQL query language transpiler and runner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B dql
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dql
compiles DelightQL \(em a query language with left-to-right pipe flow
(\fB|>\fR) \(em to SQL and optionally executes it. SQLite is spoken
natively; other engines (postgres, duckdb) are reached through separate
per-engine adapter binaries ("fatboys") managed by
.BR dql-target (1).
.PP
Invoked with no command,
.B dql
behaves exactly as
.B dql query
with no arguments: on a terminal it starts the interactive REPL;
with piped stdin it reads and executes the piped source, so
.B "dql < queries.dql"
and
.B "dql query < queries.dql"
are the same command.
.PP
Without a
.B \-\-db
option, commands operate on an ephemeral in-memory SQLite database.
Anonymous tables make this useful on its own:
.B "dql query '_(1,2;3,4)'"
needs no database at all.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR query ", " q
Compile and execute a query from an argument, a file, or stdin. The
workhorse. See
.BR dql-query (1).
.TP
.B format
Format/prettify DelightQL source. See
.BR dql-format (1).
.TP
.BR tools ", " t
Ad-hoc data munging: query JSON or CSV piped on stdin, or files loaded
as tables. See
.BR dql-tools (1).
.TP
.B explain
Explain a DelightQL identifier (error, danger gate, or config) from the
built-in registry. See
.BR dql-explain (1).
.TP
.B target
Manage per-engine adapter binaries. See
.BR dql-target (1).
.TP
.B server
Serve the relay protocol on a Unix socket. See
.BR dql-server (1).
.TP
.B version
Print build identity; machine-readable with
.BR \-\-json .
See
.BR dql-version (1).
.TP
.B selftest
Run self-diagnostics: every diagnostic provider (autoload health,
catalog orphans) reports findings as
.B delightql-diagnostic://
badged records, each explainable via
.BR "dql explain" .
.B \-\-json
emits the findings as a JSON array for CI;
.B \-\-strict
treats warnings as failures (exit nonzero on any WARN). Exit status is
nonzero on any FAIL.
.TP
.B man
Show one of these manual pages, rendered from the copies embedded in
the binary (a projection of
.IR sys::help.man_page(*) ).
Name tokens hyphen-join, so
.B dql man dql target
and
.B dql man target
both reach
.BR dql-target (1);
a leading number selects a section. On a terminal, rendering hands the
troff (via a temporary file, so BSD and Linux man both work) to
.BR man ,
falling back to groff, then to embedded plain text. When stdout is a
pipe or file, the embedded plain text is emitted directly \(em
byte-identical on every platform \(em so
.B dql man query | bat
composes as expected.
.B \-\-dump
.I DIR
writes every embedded troff page into
.I DIR
(for packaging and MANPATH installs). To search pages, query them:
.EX
$ dql query 'sys::help.man_page(*), +like(plain, "%adapter%")'
.EE
.TP
.B help
.B dql help
.I COMMAND
shows the same page as
.B dql man
.IR COMMAND ;
one mechanism, so the two can never drift apart. Without a command it
prints the usage summary (same as
.BR \-\-help ).
.TP
.B completions
Generate shell completions to stdout
.RB ( bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " elvish ", " powershell ):
.EX
$ dql completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/dql
.EE
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These may be given before or after the subcommand. A global option the
chosen subcommand cannot consume is refused, not silently ignored
.RB ( \-\-db " means nothing to " "dql version" ).
.B \-\-error\-prefix
and
.B \-\-error\-format
apply everywhere;
.B \-\-db
applies to query and server;
.B \-\-make\-new\-db\-if\-missing
to query (and bare
.BR dql ,
which is query);
.B \-\-dialect
to query, tools, and server;
.B \-\-via
to query.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " DATABASE"
SQLite database file to operate on. Optional; the default is an
in-memory database. If the named file does not exist, query refuses
unless
.B \-\-make\-new\-db\-if\-missing
is given \(em a typo'd path silently opening an empty database is a
silent wrong.
.TP
.B \-\-make\-new\-db\-if\-missing
With
.BR \-\-db :
create the database file if it does not exist. Requires
.B \-\-db
(alone it configures nothing and is refused). Works at the bare door
too:
.B "dql --db new.db --make-new-db-if-missing"
starts the REPL on a freshly created database.
.TP
.BI \-\-dialect " DIALECT"
Target SQL dialect for generated SQL: one of
.BR sqlite " (default, canonical), " postgres ", " mysql ", " sqlserver ", " duckdb .
Spellings come from the dialect_render targeting table. Equivalent to
setting
.BR DQL_DIALECT .
An unrecognized value is a hard usage error;
.B postgresql
is accepted as an alias for postgres.
.TP
.BI \-\-via " MECHANISM"
Mechanism override for reaching a postgres resource:
.B fatboy
(adapter co-process, default) or
.B siso
(pipe-wrapped psql). Resources name WHAT to reach;
.B \-\-via
chooses HOW.
.TP
.BI \-\-error\-prefix " PREFIX"
Prefix for structured error records on stderr. Default is a single
ASCII RS byte (0x1E). Records have the form:
.IP
.EX
<prefix>[delightql-error://<hierarchy>] message
.EE
.IP
Set to any string for custom scripting, e.g.
.BR "\-\-error\-prefix '@error '" .
.TP
.BI \-\-error\-format " FORMAT"
Body format of the structured error records:
.B text
(default,
.IR "[uri] message" )
or
.B json
.RI ( '{"uri": ..., "message": ...}' ,
uri null when the error carries no identity). With the default RS
prefix, json mode is exactly RFC 7464 \(em JSON text sequences, which
.B jq \-\-seq
reads directly. Additive fields may appear in later versions;
consumers must tolerate them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Compile or runtime error; a structured error record is emitted on
stderr (see
.BR \-\-error\-prefix ).
Internal crashes (Rust panics) are caught and reported the same way,
as
.IR delightql\-error://internal/panic ,
never as a raw backtrace with exit 101; set
.B RUST_BACKTRACE=1
for the developer trace.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (unknown flag or invalid value).
.PP
Dedicated gate flags may document additional codes \(em see
.BR dql\-format (1)
.RB ( \-\-fail\-if\-not\-formatted :
2 = cannot verify).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DQL_DIALECT
Same effect as
.BR \-\-dialect .
An unrecognized value refuses at startup with exit 1 \(em an ignored
explicit override would be a silent wrong.
.TP
.B DQL_FATBOY_DIR
Hard-pins the directory searched for adapter binaries, overriding all
other resolution steps. See
.BR dql-target (1).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set (any value), color auto-detection yields no color
(no-color.org convention). An explicit
.B \-\-color always
still wins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/delightql/fatboys/<version>
The adapter store, one directory per dql version.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query an SQLite file:
.PP
.EX
$ dql query --db app.db 'users(*), age > 30 |> (id, name)'
.EE
.PP
Show the SQL a query compiles to:
.PP
.EX
$ dql query --db app.db --to sql 'users(*), age > 30'
.EE
.PP
Query a CSV from stdin:
.PP
.EX
$ cat people.csv | dql tools csvstruct --has-headers 'c(*), age > 26'
.EE
.PP
Ask what an error identifier means:
.PP
.EX
$ dql explain semantic/resolution/table
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql-query (1),
.BR dql-format (1),
.BR dql-tools (1),
.BR dql-explain (1),
.BR dql-target (1),
.BR dql-server (1),
.BR dql-version (1)
